From 18306d36760dc0b08fd932323f68bf7e73683264 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EmberGate <jebadiahgreenwood@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:34:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] qwen35 : optional n-branch gated residual
 (<arch>.residual_streams) (EmberGate R5/S2)

A qwen35 GGUF may carry <arch>.residual_streams = n (> 1) and <arch>.residual_rank = r, plus per FILE trunk
layer N eight F32 tensors blk.N.hc_mix.{gain,w_a,w_u,w_v} and blk.N.hc_mlp.{gain,w_a,w_u,w_v}. The trunk then
carries the residual as n branches S [n_embd, n, T] (the embedding fanned out n times). Around each sub-block
(mixer, MLP):
  read : Rh = rms_norm(S) * gain, v = Rh as [n*n_embd, T], G = 2*sigmoid(W_u silu(W_a v / n)),
         x = mean_i (G * Rh)_i (the sub-block input), s = 2*sigmoid(W_v v / n) [n, T]
  write: S_i += s_i * y (y = the unchanged sub-block output)
After the last layer h = mean_i S_i goes to output_norm; output_norm(h) is also the MTP head's input
(t_h_nextn), as in the HF reference (archmods.MergeNorm merges before the final norm). The MTP block itself keeps
its plain residual. With <arch>.layer_schedule a repeated position uses its file layer's gates (shared, like its
other weights). Only existing ggml ops (rms_norm, mul, mul_mat, sigmoid, silu, scale, repeat, add, views).

No key: the plain loop is built exactly as before (logit files byte-identical on the plain and the scheduled a50).
